## Course Overview

This course gives a fundamental idea about the common theoretical phenomena in advanced Object-Oriented Programming using Java. It also provides a bridge to students' previous knowledge of Object-Oriented Programming.

**Course Code:** CSE 0613-3121 | **Credit:** 3.00 | **Total Marks:** 100

## Course Objectives

- Familiarize students with the advanced level of the Object-Oriented paradigm
- Help them know the basic structure of an Object-Oriented Programming language
- Make them understand Object-Oriented concepts in practice
- Make students able to understand the relation between classes and objects with access control
- Understand the use of various OOP concepts and how to apply them to real scenarios

## Course Learning Outcomes (CLOs)

After successful completion of the course, students will be able to:

- **CLO1.** Understand the features of Advanced Object-Oriented Programming
- **CLO2.** Identify classes, objects, members of a class and the relationships among them
- **CLO3.** Develop Java application programs using OOP principles and program structuring
- **CLO4.** Demonstrate the concepts of OOP
- **CLO5.** Gain OOP and Java knowledge in solving problems
- **CLO6.** Use Java GUI and Java Applet
- **CLO7.** Demonstrate a commitment to lifelong learning and professional development by engaging in independent learning and staying updated with advancements in computer science and programming languages

